id: pauls-letters
title: Paul's letters
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The thirteen letters that bear Paul's name, Romans to Philemon, in
  the order they are printed, one chapter a reading: 87 readings.
suits: Readers who want to read Paul's letters slowly, a chapter at a
  sitting of two or three minutes, on five days a week.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 5
coverage: books
canon: protestant
books: ROM, 1CO, 2CO, GAL, EPH, PHP, COL, 1TH, 2TH, 1TI, 2TI, TIT, PHM
limitations: It reads these thirteen letters only. Hebrews, which does not
  name its author and which some have counted among Paul's letters, is not
  in it. The letters are read in the order they are printed, not the order
  in which they were written, which is debated; the plan takes no side on
  it. Chapters differ in length, from about a minute to about six.
instructions: Read one chapter on each of your five reading days, in any
  Bible; the other two days of the week are rest days. If you miss a day,
  your next reading waits for you. At five readings a week the plan takes
  about four months.
source: An original plan by Day by Word: the chapters of the thirteen
  letters that open with Paul's name, in printed order, one a reading.
  Reading times are estimated from word counts of the World English Bible,
  a public-domain translation; the plan can be read in any translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
